Goals
* Implement a reverse proxy to centralize access to internal Docker services.
* Introduce HTTPS encrpytion for internal applications. 
* Prepare my lab for identity-based access control.
* Maintain full isolation from my home network. 

Tools
* Raspberry Pi 5
* Docker
* Docker Compose
* Portainer
* Nginx
* openSSL

What I Did
* Created a dedicated Docker network to allow internal communication. 
* Deployed Nginx Proxy Manager using Docker Compose. 
* Configured custom port mappings to avoid conflict with exsisting services. 
* Attatched the Portainer container to the dedicated network to allow name based routing. 
* Created a proxy host in NPM to forward traffic to the portainer by container name. 
* Enabled WebSocket support and basic exploit protection in proxy settings. 
* Generated a self signed certificate using openSSL.
* Configured TLS terminatino at the proxy layer and enabled forced HTTPS. 

Why
* Used a reverse proxy to create a single controlled entry point to internal services.
* Eliminated direct IP:port access patterns and moved toward centralized routing. 
* Implemented TLS termination at the proxy layer to simulate enterpise load balancing behavior. 
* Maintinaed full lab isolation by avoiding router level changes. 
* Built the foudnaitno for me to impelemnt MFA and identity based access control.

Problems
* Port Conflict
  - Docker failed to start NPM becuase port 80 was already in use.
  - Identified the conflict as an exsisting service, my pihole was binded to port 80.
  - Resolved by remapping Nginx ports to 8080 and 8443 instead of modifying my pihole or router settings. 
*502 Error
  - Initial proxy configuraiton returned 502 errors.
  - Identifed the issue as a misspelling in the Forward Hostname field, reiterating the importance of being careful.
* SSL Cert
  - Had to manually generate a self signed certiface for interal HTTPS. 
  - Generated key and certifcate using openSSL.
  - Transfered the certifiacete files from the pi to my local machine
  - Uploaded certificate and key into NPM and applied to my proxy host. 

Learned
* How reverse proxies route traffic based on domain name and upstream container name.
* How TLS termination works at the proxy layer. 
* How Docker container networking enables internal name based communication.
* The difference between host level ports and container level ports.
* How loal DNS resolution impacts reverse proxy routing behavior. 
